A||||9||avengador1||Here is how I got rid of blind spots in my car||||10||
Z||000000||avengador1||11-04-2001||01:48 PM||||I used to have one of these in one of my past cars. I found that J.C.Whitney still has the 3 and 4 panel Wink mirrors. With these you almost get 360 degree vision. They take a little getting used to but offer a panoramic view. I remember seeing these in a lot of race cars. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Camer020.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||avengador1||11-04-2001||01:50 PM||||Another view of my Wink mirror. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Camer021.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||11-04-2001||01:53 PM||||Great add-on huh??  I have a 5 panel wink in mine.. I had it in my 87GT before I got slammed in the passenger door.. Now I have it in the Smoooooth GT..  I have a HUGE  blind spot in the Smoooooth GT as you could imagine.. also I have NO SIDE MIRROR'S EITHER, so the blind spot is even bigger then most, but with the Wink.. I can see everything around me!!!  Steve<P>ps. The 5 panel is about 6-8" from the side of the windshield.. almost all the way across the window!!<BR>------------------<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Yellow_sig.gif">     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig_blue.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Smoooooth GT (edited 11-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||avengador1||11-04-2001||02:30 PM||||I wanted a 5 panel but could not find one.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Screwie||11-04-2001||03:02 PM||||Wow, I've never seen those kind of things!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> Does it look good? Or is it just for more sight?  I'd have to get used to those things up there! But, the more you can see not just around but also of your Fiero, the better and in those things you can admire your rearwing all the time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||MrPBody||11-04-2001||04:08 PM||||I like it.  I have a 5-panel in my '85 SE.  It's great being able to see all the way around!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||avengador1||11-04-2001||04:17 PM||||From the first picture you can get an idea as to how much more you can see. It also makes it easier to see over the rear spoiler.||||reg||1
Z||000007||88CoupeV6||11-04-2001||05:32 PM||||The 1st thing I do on all my Fiero's is add one inch round spot mirrors to the outside mirrors. Cuts out the blind spots and is great on the highway for changing lanes with confidence. I would never trust mirrors without them. I think that all cars should come stock with them. It only makes sense. <P>I will take pics when it is light out.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I hate this time of year when it is dark at 5:00PM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gerald||11-04-2001||05:46 PM||||Where do I get one? I want I want  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
